---@field Source aws.rds.DatabaseArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the source production database.
---@field TargetEngineVersion? aws.rds.TargetEngineVersion The engine version of the database in the green environment.
---@field TargetDBParameterGroupName? aws.rds.TargetDBParameterGroupName The DB parameter group associated with the DB instance in the green environment.
---@field TargetDBClusterParameterGroupName? aws.rds.TargetDBClusterParameterGroupName The DB cluster parameter group associated with the Aurora DB cluster in the green environment.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList Tags to assign to the blue/green deployment.
---@field TargetDBInstanceClass? aws.rds.TargetDBInstanceClass Specify the DB instance class for the databases in the green environment.
---@field UpgradeTargetStorageConfig? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Whether to upgrade the storage file system configuration on the green database. This option migrates the green DB instance from the older 32-bit file system to the preferred configuration. For more information, see Upgrading the storage file system for a DB instance.
---@field TargetIops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of Provisioned IOPS (input/output operations per second) to allocate for the green DB instance. For information about valid IOPS values, see Amazon RDS DB instance storage in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field TargetStorageType? aws.rds.TargetStorageType The storage type to associate with the green DB instance.
---@field TargetAllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of storage in gibibytes (GiB) to allocate for the green DB instance. You can choose to increase or decrease the allocated storage on the green DB instance.
