---@class aws.rds.CreateCustomDBEngineVersionMessage
---@field Engine aws.rds.CustomEngineName The database engine.
---@field EngineVersion aws.rds.CustomEngineVersion The name of your custom engine version (CEV).
---@field DatabaseInstallationFilesS3BucketName? aws.rds.BucketName The name of an Amazon S3 bucket that contains database installation files for your CEV. For example, a valid bucket name is my-custom-installation-files.
---@field DatabaseInstallationFilesS3Prefix? aws.rds.String255 The Amazon S3 directory that contains the database installation files for your CEV. For example, a valid bucket name is 123456789012/cev1. If this setting isn't specified, no prefix is assumed.
---@field DatabaseInstallationFiles? aws.rds.StringList The database installation files (ISO and EXE) uploaded to Amazon S3 for your database engine version to import to Amazon RDS.
---@field ImageId? aws.rds.String255 The ID of the Amazon Machine Image (AMI). For RDS Custom for SQL Server, an AMI ID is required to create a CEV. For RDS Custom for Oracle, the default is the most recent AMI available, but you can specify an AMI ID that was used in a different Oracle CEV. Find the AMIs used by your CEVs by calling the DescribeDBEngineVersions operation.
---@field KMSKeyId? aws.rds.KmsKeyIdOrArn The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for an encrypted CEV. A symmetric encryption KMS key is required for RDS Custom, but optional for Amazon RDS.
---@field SourceCustomDbEngineVersionIdentifier? aws.rds.String255 The ARN of a CEV to use as a source for creating a new CEV. You can specify a different Amazon Machine Imagine (AMI) by using either Source or UseAwsProvidedLatestImage. You can't specify a different JSON manifest when you specify SourceCustomDbEngineVersionIdentifier.
---@field UseAwsProvidedLatestImage? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to use the latest service-provided Amazon Machine Image (AMI) for the CEV. If you specify UseAwsProvidedLatestImage, you can't also specify ImageId.
---@field Description? aws.rds.Description An optional description of your CEV.
---@field Manifest? aws.rds.CustomDBEngineVersionManifest The CEV manifest, which is a JSON document that describes the installation .zip files stored in Amazon S3. Specify the name/value pairs in a file or a quoted string. RDS Custom applies the patches in the order in which they are listed.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBCapacityReservationRequest
---@field DBCapacityReservationName aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationName The name of the DB capacity reservation. This name must be unique for your Amazon Web Services account in the Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field DBInstanceClass aws.rds.DBInstanceClass The compute and memory capacity to reserve, for example db.m5.large. Not all DB instance classes are available in all Amazon Web Services Regions, or for all database engines. For the full list of DB instance classes, and availability for your engine, see DB instance classes in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field Engine aws.rds.String The database engine to reserve capacity for.
---@field CapacityPerAvailabilityZone aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of DB instances to reserve in each Availability Zone that you list in AvailabilityZones. Amazon RDS reserves this number of DB instances in every listed Availability Zone.
---@field AvailabilityZones aws.rds.AvailabilityZones A list of Availability Zones for the reservation.
---@field EndDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the reservation expires, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). If you don't specify a value, the reservation doesn't expire.
---@field StartDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the reservation starts, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). Specify this parameter to create a future-dated reservation. If you don't specify a value, the reservation starts immediately.
---@field CommitmentDuration? aws.rds.LongOptional The length of the capacity commitment that you request for a future-dated reservation, in seconds. Amazon RDS measures this length from StartDate.
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String The license model to reserve capacity for. Specify this parameter only for RDS for Microsoft SQL Server Enterprise Edition, Standard Edition, and Developer Edition, for RDS for Oracle, or for RDS for Db2 Standard Edition and Advanced Edition. Amazon RDS rejects the request for any other engine. This includes Amazon Aurora, the Web and Express editions of RDS for Microsoft SQL Server, and RDS for D...
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList Tags to assign to the DB capacity reservation.

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBCapacityReservationResponse
---@field DBCapacityReservation? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservation Contains the details of the newly created DB capacity reservation.

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBClusterEndpointMessage
---@field DBClusterIdentifier aws.rds.String The DB cluster identifier of the DB cluster associated with the endpoint. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field DBClusterEndpointIdentifier aws.rds.String The identifier to use for the new endpoint. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field EndpointType aws.rds.String The type of the endpoint, one of: READER, WRITER, ANY.
---@field StaticMembers? aws.rds.StringList List of DB instance identifiers that are part of the custom endpoint group.
---@field ExcludedMembers? aws.rds.StringList List of DB instance identifiers that aren't part of the custom endpoint group. All other eligible instances are reachable through the custom endpoint. This parameter is relevant only if the list of static members is empty.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList The tags to be assigned to the Amazon RDS resource.

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBClusterMessage
---@field AvailabilityZones? aws.rds.AvailabilityZones A list of Availability Zones (AZs) where you specifically want to create DB instances in the DB cluster.
---@field BackupRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days for which automated backups are retained.
---@field CharacterSetName? aws.rds.String The name of the character set (CharacterSet) to associate the DB cluster with.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.rds.String The name for your database of up to 64 alphanumeric characters. A database named postgres is always created. If this parameter is specified, an additional database with this name is created.
---@field DBClusterIdentifier aws.rds.String The identifier for this DB cluster. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field DBClusterParameterGroupName? aws.rds.String The name of the DB cluster parameter group to associate with this DB cluster. If you don't specify a value, then the default DB cluster parameter group for the specified DB engine and version is used.
---@field VpcSecurityGroupIds? aws.rds.VpcSecurityGroupIdList A list of EC2 VPC security groups to associate with this DB cluster.
---@field DBSubnetGroupName? aws.rds.String A DB subnet group to associate with this DB cluster.
---@field Engine aws.rds.String The database engine to use for this DB cluster.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String The version number of the database engine to use.
---@field Port? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The port number on which the instances in the DB cluster accept connections.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.rds.String The name of the master user for the DB cluster.
---@field MasterUserPassword? aws.rds.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret The password for the master database user.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String The option group to associate the DB cluster with.
---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled using the BackupRetentionPeriod parameter.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.rds.String The weekly time range during which system maintenance can occur.
---@field ReplicationSourceIdentifier? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the source DB instance or DB cluster if this DB cluster is created as a read replica.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList Tags to assign to the DB cluster.
---@field StorageEncrypted? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB cluster is encrypted.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for an encrypted DB cluster.
---@field PreSignedUrl? aws.rds.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret When you are replicating a DB cluster from one Amazon Web Services GovCloud (US) Region to another, an URL that contains a Signature Version 4 signed request for the CreateDBCluster operation to be called in the source Amazon Web Services Region where the DB cluster is replicated from. Specify PreSignedUrl only when you are performing cross-Region replication from an encrypted DB cluster.
---@field EnableIAMDatabaseAuthentication? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts. By default, mapping isn't enabled.
---@field BacktrackWindow? aws.rds.LongOptional The target backtrack window, in seconds. To disable backtracking, set this value to 0.
---@field EnableCloudwatchLogsExports? aws.rds.LogTypeList The list of log types that need to be enabled for exporting to CloudWatch Logs.
---@field EngineMode? aws.rds.String The DB engine mode of the DB cluster, either provisioned or serverless.
---@field ScalingConfiguration? aws.rds.ScalingConfiguration For DB clusters in serverless DB engine mode, the scaling properties of the DB cluster.
---@field RdsCustomClusterConfiguration? aws.rds.RdsCustomClusterConfiguration Reserved for future use.
---@field DBClusterInstanceClass? aws.rds.String The compute and memory capacity of each DB instance in the Multi-AZ DB cluster, for example db.m6gd.xlarge. Not all DB instance classes are available in all Amazon Web Services Regions, or for all database engines.
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of storage in gibibytes (GiB) to allocate to each DB instance in the Multi-AZ DB cluster.
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String The storage type to associate with the DB cluster.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of Provisioned IOPS (input/output operations per second) to be initially allocated for each DB instance in the Multi-AZ DB cluster.
---@field PubliclyAccessible? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB cluster is publicly accessible.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether minor engine upgrades are applied automatically to the DB cluster during the maintenance window. By default, minor engine upgrades are applied automatically.
---@field DeletionProtection? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB cluster has deletion protection enabled. The database can't be deleted when deletion protection is enabled. By default, deletion protection isn't enabled.
---@field GlobalClusterIdentifier? aws.rds.GlobalClusterIdentifier The global cluster ID of an Aurora cluster that becomes the primary cluster in the new global database cluster.
---@field EnableHttpEndpoint? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable the HTTP endpoint for the DB cluster. By default, the HTTP endpoint isn't enabled.
---@field CopyTagsToSnapshot? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to copy all tags from the DB cluster to snapshots of the DB cluster. The default is not to copy them.
---@field Domain? aws.rds.String The Active Directory directory ID to create the DB cluster in.
---@field DomainIAMRoleName? aws.rds.String The name of the IAM role to use when making API calls to the Directory Service.
---@field EnableGlobalWriteForwarding? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable this DB cluster to forward write operations to the primary cluster of a global cluster (Aurora global database). By default, write operations are not allowed on Aurora DB clusters that are secondary clusters in an Aurora global database.
---@field NetworkType? aws.rds.String The network type of the DB cluster.
---@field ServerlessV2ScalingConfiguration? aws.rds.ServerlessV2ScalingConfiguration
---@field MonitoringInterval? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The interval, in seconds, between points when Enhanced Monitoring metrics are collected for the DB cluster. To turn off collecting Enhanced Monitoring metrics, specify 0.
---@field MonitoringRoleArn? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the IAM role that permits RDS to send Enhanced Monitoring metrics to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An example is arn:aws:iam:123456789012:role/emaccess. For information on creating a monitoring role, see Setting up and enabling Enhanced Monitoring in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field DatabaseInsightsMode? aws.rds.DatabaseInsightsMode|string The mode of Database Insights to enable for the DB cluster.
---@field EnablePerformanceInsights? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to turn on Performance Insights for the DB cluster.
---@field PerformanceInsightsKMSKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for encryption of Performance Insights data.
---@field PerformanceInsightsRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days to retain Performance Insights data.
---@field EnableLimitlessDatabase? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable Aurora Limitless Database. You must enable Aurora Limitless Database to create a DB shard group.
---@field ClusterScalabilityType? aws.rds.ClusterScalabilityType|string Specifies the scalability mode of the Aurora DB cluster. When set to limitless, the cluster operates as an Aurora Limitless Database. When set to standard (the default), the cluster uses normal DB instance creation.
---@field DBSystemId? aws.rds.String Reserved for future use.
---@field ManageMasterUserPassword? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to manage the master user password with Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager.
---@field EnableLocalWriteForwarding? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether read replicas can forward write operations to the writer DB instance in the DB cluster. By default, write operations aren't allowed on reader DB instances.
---@field MasterUserSecretKmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier to encrypt a secret that is automatically generated and managed in Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager.
---@field CACertificateIdentifier? aws.rds.String The CA certificate identifier to use for the DB cluster's server certificate.
---@field EngineLifecycleSupport? aws.rds.String The lifecycle type for this DB cluster.
---@field TagSpecifications? aws.rds.TagSpecificationList Tags to assign to resources associated with the DB cluster.
---@field MasterUserAuthenticationType? aws.rds.MasterUserAuthenticationType|string Specifies the authentication type for the master user. With IAM master user authentication, you can configure the master DB user with IAM database authentication when you create a DB cluster.
---@field WithExpressConfiguration? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies to create an Aurora DB Cluster with express configuration in seconds. Express configuration provides a cluster with a writer instance and feature specific values set to all other input parameters of this API.
---@field AssociatedRoles? aws.rds.DBClusterAssociatedRoles A list of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) roles to associate with the DB cluster. Each role grants the DB cluster permission to access other Amazon Web Services on your behalf. For each role, specify a role ARN and, optionally, the feature name (such as s3Import, s3Export, or Lambda).

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBClusterParameterGroupMessage
