---@class aws.rds.CreateDBInstanceMessage
---@field DBName? aws.rds.String The meaning of this parameter differs according to the database engine you use.
---@field DBInstanceIdentifier aws.rds.String The identifier for this DB instance. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of storage in gibibytes (GiB) to allocate for the DB instance.
---@field DBInstanceClass aws.rds.String The compute and memory capacity of the DB instance, for example db.m5.large. Not all DB instance classes are available in all Amazon Web Services Regions, or for all database engines. For the full list of DB instance classes, and availability for your engine, see DB instance classes in the Amazon RDS User Guide or Aurora DB instance classes in the Amazon Aurora User Guide.
---@field Engine aws.rds.String The database engine to use for this DB instance.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.rds.String The name for the master user.
---@field MasterUserPassword? aws.rds.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret The password for the master user.
---@field DBSecurityGroups? aws.rds.DBSecurityGroupNameList A list of DB security groups to associate with this DB instance.
---@field VpcSecurityGroupIds? aws.rds.VpcSecurityGroupIdList A list of Amazon EC2 VPC security groups to associate with this DB instance.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.rds.String The Availability Zone (AZ) where the database will be created. For information on Amazon Web Services Regions and Availability Zones, see Regions and Availability Zones.
---@field DBSubnetGroupName? aws.rds.String A DB subnet group to associate with this DB instance.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.rds.String The time range each week during which system maintenance can occur. For more information, see Amazon RDS Maintenance Window in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field DBParameterGroupName? aws.rds.String The name of the DB parameter group to associate with this DB instance. If you don't specify a value, then Amazon RDS uses the default DB parameter group for the specified DB engine and version.
---@field BackupRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days for which automated backups are retained. Setting this parameter to a positive number enables backups. Setting this parameter to 0 disables automated backups.
---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled, using the BackupRetentionPeriod parameter. The default is a 30-minute window selected at random from an 8-hour block of time for each Amazon Web Services Region. For more information, see Backup window in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field Port? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The port number on which the database accepts connections.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance is a Multi-AZ deployment. You can't set the AvailabilityZone parameter if the DB instance is a Multi-AZ deployment.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String The version number of the database engine to use.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether minor engine upgrades are applied automatically to the DB instance during the maintenance window. By default, minor engine upgrades are applied automatically.
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String The license model information for this DB instance.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of Provisioned IOPS (input/output operations per second) to initially allocate for the DB instance. For information about valid IOPS values, see Amazon RDS DB instance storage in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field StorageThroughput? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The storage throughput value, in mebibyte per second (MiBps), for the DB instance.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String The option group to associate the DB instance with.
---@field CharacterSetName? aws.rds.String For supported engines, the character set (CharacterSet) to associate the DB instance with.
---@field NcharCharacterSetName? aws.rds.String The name of the NCHAR character set for the Oracle DB instance.
---@field PubliclyAccessible? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance is publicly accessible.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList Tags to assign to the DB instance.
---@field DBClusterIdentifier? aws.rds.String The identifier of the DB cluster that this DB instance will belong to.
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String The storage type to associate with the DB instance.
---@field TdeCredentialArn? aws.rds.String The ARN from the key store with which to associate the instance for TDE encryption.
---@field TdeCredentialPassword? aws.rds.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret The password for the given ARN from the key store in order to access the device.
---@field StorageEncrypted? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifes whether the DB instance is encrypted. By default, it isn't encrypted.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for an encrypted DB instance.
---@field Domain? aws.rds.String The Active Directory directory ID to create the DB instance in. Currently, you can create only Db2, MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, Oracle, and PostgreSQL DB instances in an Active Directory Domain.
---@field DomainFqdn? aws.rds.String The fully qualified domain name (FQDN) of an Active Directory domain.
---@field DomainOu? aws.rds.String The Active Directory organizational unit for your DB instance to join.
---@field DomainAuthSecretArn? aws.rds.String The ARN for the Secrets Manager secret with the credentials for the user joining the domain.
---@field DomainDnsIps? aws.rds.StringList The IPv4 DNS IP addresses of your primary and secondary Active Directory domain controllers.
---@field CopyTagsToSnapshot? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to copy tags from the DB instance to snapshots of the DB instance. By default, tags are not copied.
---@field MonitoringInterval? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The interval, in seconds, between points when Enhanced Monitoring metrics are collected for the DB instance. To disable collection of Enhanced Monitoring metrics, specify 0.
---@field MonitoringRoleArn? aws.rds.String The ARN for the IAM role that permits RDS to send enhanced monitoring metrics to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. For example, arn:aws:iam:123456789012:role/emaccess. For information on creating a monitoring role, see Setting Up and Enabling Enhanced Monitoring in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field DomainIAMRoleName? aws.rds.String The name of the IAM role to use when making API calls to the Directory Service.
---@field PromotionTier? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The order of priority in which an Aurora Replica is promoted to the primary instance after a failure of the existing primary instance. For more information, see Fault Tolerance for an Aurora DB Cluster in the Amazon Aurora User Guide.
---@field Timezone? aws.rds.String The time zone of the DB instance. The time zone parameter is currently supported only by RDS for Db2 and RDS for SQL Server.
---@field EnableIAMDatabaseAuthentication? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts. By default, mapping isn't enabled.
---@field DatabaseInsightsMode? aws.rds.DatabaseInsightsMode|string The mode of Database Insights to enable for the DB instance.
---@field EnablePerformanceInsights? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable Performance Insights for the DB instance. For more information, see Using Amazon Performance Insights in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field PerformanceInsightsKMSKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for encryption of Performance Insights data.
---@field PerformanceInsightsRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days to retain Performance Insights data.
---@field EnableCloudwatchLogsExports? aws.rds.LogTypeList The list of log types to enable for exporting to CloudWatch Logs. For more information, see Publishing Database Logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field ProcessorFeatures? aws.rds.ProcessorFeatureList The number of CPU cores and the number of threads per core for the DB instance class of the DB instance.
---@field DeletionProtection? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance has deletion protection enabled. The database can't be deleted when deletion protection is enabled. By default, deletion protection isn't enabled. For more information, see Deleting a DB Instance.
---@field MaxAllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The upper limit in gibibytes (GiB) to which Amazon RDS can automatically scale the storage of the DB instance.
---@field EnableCustomerOwnedIp? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable a customer-owned IP address (CoIP) for an RDS on Outposts DB instance.
---@field NetworkType? aws.rds.String The network type of the DB instance.
---@field BackupTarget? aws.rds.String The location for storing automated backups and manual snapshots.
---@field CustomIamInstanceProfile? aws.rds.String The instance profile associated with the underlying Amazon EC2 instance of an RDS Custom DB instance.
---@field DBSystemId? aws.rds.String The Oracle system identifier (SID), which is the name of the Oracle database instance that manages your database files. In this context, the term "Oracle database instance" refers exclusively to the system global area (SGA) and Oracle background processes. If you don't specify a SID, the value defaults to RDSCDB. The Oracle SID is also the name of your CDB.
---@field CACertificateIdentifier? aws.rds.String The CA certificate identifier to use for the DB instance's server certificate.
---@field ManageMasterUserPassword? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to manage the master user password with Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager.
---@field MasterUserSecretKmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier to encrypt a secret that is automatically generated and managed in Amazon Web Services Secrets Manager.
---@field MultiTenant? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to use the multi-tenant configuration or the single-tenant configuration (default). This parameter only applies to RDS for Oracle container database (CDB) engines.
---@field DedicatedLogVolume? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV) enabled.
---@field EngineLifecycleSupport? aws.rds.String The lifecycle type for this DB instance.
---@field AdditionalStorageVolumes? aws.rds.AdditionalStorageVolumesList A list of additional storage volumes to create for the DB instance. You can create up to three additional storage volumes using the names rdsdbdata2, rdsdbdata3, and rdsdbdata4. Additional storage volumes are supported for RDS for Oracle and RDS for SQL Server DB instances only.
---@field TagSpecifications? aws.rds.TagSpecificationList Tags to assign to resources associated with the DB instance.
---@field DBCapacityReservationIdentifier? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationIdentifier The identifier or the name of the DB capacity reservation to associate with this DB instance. You can specify the identifier, which has the prefix dbcr-, or the reservation name. When you specify this parameter, the DB instance uses reserved capacity from the specified reservation.
---@field MasterUserAuthenticationType? aws.rds.MasterUserAuthenticationType|string Specifies the authentication type for the master user. With IAM master user authentication, you can configure the master DB user with IAM database authentication when you create a DB instance.

---@class aws.rds.CreateDBInstanceReadReplicaMessage
---@field DBInstanceIdentifier aws.rds.String The DB instance identifier of the read replica. This identifier is the unique key that identifies a DB instance. This parameter is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field SourceDBInstanceIdentifier? aws.rds.String The identifier of the DB instance that will act as the source for the read replica. Each DB instance can have up to 15 read replicas, except for the following engines:
---@field DBInstanceClass? aws.rds.String The compute and memory capacity of the read replica, for example db.m4.large. Not all DB instance classes are available in all Amazon Web Services Regions, or for all database engines. For the full list of DB instance classes, and availability for your engine, see DB Instance Class in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.rds.String The Availability Zone (AZ) where the read replica will be created.
---@field Port? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The port number that the DB instance uses for connections.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the read replica is in a Multi-AZ deployment.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to automatically apply minor engine upgrades to the read replica during the maintenance window.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of Provisioned IOPS (input/output operations per second) to initially allocate for the DB instance.
---@field StorageThroughput? aws.rds.IntegerOptional Specifies the storage throughput value for the read replica.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String The option group to associate the DB instance with. If not specified, RDS uses the option group associated with the source DB instance or cluster.
---@field DBParameterGroupName? aws.rds.String The name of the DB parameter group to associate with this read replica DB instance.
---@field PubliclyAccessible? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance is publicly accessible.
---@field Tags? aws.rds.TagList
---@field DBSubnetGroupName? aws.rds.String A DB subnet group for the DB instance. The new DB instance is created in the VPC associated with the DB subnet group. If no DB subnet group is specified, then the new DB instance isn't created in a VPC.
---@field VpcSecurityGroupIds? aws.rds.VpcSecurityGroupIdList A list of Amazon EC2 VPC security groups to associate with the read replica.
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String The storage type to associate with the read replica.
---@field CopyTagsToSnapshot? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to copy all tags from the read replica to snapshots of the read replica. By default, tags aren't copied.
---@field MonitoringInterval? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The interval, in seconds, between points when Enhanced Monitoring metrics are collected for the read replica. To disable collection of Enhanced Monitoring metrics, specify 0. The default is 0.
---@field MonitoringRoleArn? aws.rds.String The ARN for the IAM role that permits RDS to send enhanced monitoring metrics to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. For example, arn:aws:iam:123456789012:role/emaccess. For information on creating a monitoring role, go to To create an IAM role for Amazon RDS Enhanced Monitoring in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for an encrypted read replica.
---@field PreSignedUrl? aws.rds.SensitiveString|distilled.Secret When you are creating a read replica from one Amazon Web Services GovCloud (US) Region to another or from one China Amazon Web Services Region to another, the URL that contains a Signature Version 4 signed request for the CreateDBInstanceReadReplica API operation in the source Amazon Web Services Region that contains the source DB instance.
---@field EnableIAMDatabaseAuthentication? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts. By default, mapping isn't enabled.
---@field DatabaseInsightsMode? aws.rds.DatabaseInsightsMode|string The mode of Database Insights to enable for the read replica.
---@field EnablePerformanceInsights? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable Performance Insights for the read replica.
---@field PerformanceInsightsKMSKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for encryption of Performance Insights data.
---@field PerformanceInsightsRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days to retain Performance Insights data.
---@field EnableCloudwatchLogsExports? aws.rds.LogTypeList The list of logs that the new DB instance is to export to CloudWatch Logs. The values in the list depend on the DB engine being used. For more information, see Publishing Database Logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
---@field ProcessorFeatures? aws.rds.ProcessorFeatureList The number of CPU cores and the number of threads per core for the DB instance class of the DB instance.
---@field UseDefaultProcessorFeatures? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance class of the DB instance uses its default processor features.
---@field DeletionProtection? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable deletion protection for the DB instance. The database can't be deleted when deletion protection is enabled. By default, deletion protection isn't enabled. For more information, see Deleting a DB Instance.
---@field Domain? aws.rds.String The Active Directory directory ID to create the DB instance in. Currently, only MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server, Oracle, and PostgreSQL DB instances can be created in an Active Directory Domain.
---@field DomainIAMRoleName? aws.rds.String The name of the IAM role to use when making API calls to the Directory Service.
---@field DomainFqdn? aws.rds.String The fully qualified domain name (FQDN) of an Active Directory domain.
---@field DomainOu? aws.rds.String The Active Directory organizational unit for your DB instance to join.
---@field DomainAuthSecretArn? aws.rds.String The ARN for the Secrets Manager secret with the credentials for the user joining the domain.
---@field DomainDnsIps? aws.rds.StringList The IPv4 DNS IP addresses of your primary and secondary Active Directory domain controllers.
---@field ReplicaMode? aws.rds.ReplicaMode|string The open mode of the replica database.
---@field EnableCustomerOwnedIp? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether to enable a customer-owned IP address (CoIP) for an RDS on Outposts read replica.
---@field NetworkType? aws.rds.String The network type of the DB instance.
---@field MaxAllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The upper limit in gibibytes (GiB) to which Amazon RDS can automatically scale the storage of the DB instance.
---@field BackupTarget? aws.rds.String The location where RDS stores automated backups and manual snapshots.
---@field CustomIamInstanceProfile? aws.rds.String The instance profile associated with the underlying Amazon EC2 instance of an RDS Custom DB instance. The instance profile must meet the following requirements:
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The amount of storage (in gibibytes) to allocate initially for the read replica. Follow the allocation rules specified in CreateDBInstance.
---@field SourceDBClusterIdentifier? aws.rds.String The identifier of the Multi-AZ DB cluster that will act as the source for the read replica. Each DB cluster can have up to 15 read replicas.
---@field DedicatedLogVolume? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV) enabled.
---@field UpgradeStorageConfig? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Whether to upgrade the storage file system configuration on the read replica. This option migrates the read replica from the old storage file system layout to the preferred layout.
---@field CACertificateIdentifier? aws.rds.String The CA certificate identifier to use for the read replica's server certificate.
---@field AdditionalStorageVolumes? aws.rds.AdditionalStorageVolumesList A list of additional storage volumes to create for the DB instance. You can create up to three additional storage volumes using the names rdsdbdata2, rdsdbdata3, and rdsdbdata4. Additional storage volumes are supported for RDS for Oracle and RDS for SQL Server DB instances only.
---@field TagSpecifications? aws.rds.TagSpecificationList Tags to assign to resources associated with the DB instance.
---@field DBCapacityReservationIdentifier? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationIdentifier The identifier or the name of the DB capacity reservation to associate with this read replica. You can specify the identifier, which has the prefix dbcr-, or the reservation name. When you specify this parameter, the read replica uses reserved capacity from the specified reservation. A read replica uses one unit of reserved capacity, in the same way as any other DB instance.

