---Contains the details of a DB capacity reservation.
---@class aws.rds.DBCapacityReservation
---@field DBCapacityReservationName? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationName The name that you specified for the DB capacity reservation.
---@field DBInstanceClass? aws.rds.DBInstanceClass The DB instance class for the reserved capacity. You specify this value when you create the reservation, and you can't change it afterward.
---@field Engine? aws.rds.String The database engine for the reserved capacity. You specify this value when you create the reservation, and you can't change it afterward.
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String The license model for the reserved capacity. Amazon RDS returns this value only for a reservation that reserves capacity for a specific license model. Amazon RDS doesn't return this value for a reservation whose database engine doesn't support a license model.
---@field ReservedCapacityPerAvailabilityZone? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of DB instances that Amazon RDS reserves in each Availability Zone of the reservation. This value matches the CapacityPerAvailabilityZone parameter of the request. The total reserved capacity is this value multiplied by the number of Availability Zones of the reservation.
---@field AvailableCapacityPerAvailabilityZoneList? aws.rds.AvailableCapacityPerAvailabilityZoneList The unused capacity of the reservation, reported for each Availability Zone of the reservation. Each entry names one Availability Zone, and it reports the number of DB instances that remain available in that Availability Zone.
---@field EndDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the reservation expires, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). Amazon RDS doesn't return this value if the reservation doesn't expire.
---@field CreateDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the reservation was created, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC).
---@field StartDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when a future-dated reservation starts, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). Amazon RDS doesn't return this value for a reservation that started immediately.
---@field CommitmentInfo? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationCommitmentInfo The capacity commitment of the reservation. Amazon RDS returns this object only for a future-dated reservation.
---@field State? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationState The current state of the DB capacity reservation. A DB instance can use the reservation in the active state only.
---@field DBCapacityReservationArn? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the DB capacity reservation.
---@field DBCapacityReservationIdentifier? aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationIdentifier The unique identifier of the DB capacity reservation. The identifier has the prefix dbcr-. Every other DB capacity reservation operation takes this identifier.
---@field TagList? aws.rds.TagList The tags associated with the DB capacity reservation.

---Contains the capacity commitment details of a DB capacity reservation, including the number of committed DB instances in each Availability Zone and the end date of the commitment period. Amazon RDS holds the committed capacity until the commitment ends. Amazon RDS rejects a request to cancel a reservation in the active state, and a request to reduce the reserved capacity below the commitment.
---@class aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationCommitmentInfo
---@field CommittedCapacityPerAvailabilityZone? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of DB instances that Amazon RDS holds in each Availability Zone of the reservation for the length of the commitment.
---@field CommitmentEndDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the commitment ends, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC). This date reports the capacity commitment that Amazon RDS granted.

---@alias aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationIdentifier string

---@alias aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationList aws.rds.DBCapacityReservation[]

---@alias aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationName string

---@alias aws.rds.DBCapacityReservationState "active"|"expired"|"cancelled"|"pending"|"failed"|"assessing"|"scheduled"|"delayed"|"unsupported"

---Contains the details of an Amazon Aurora DB cluster or Multi-AZ DB cluster.
---@class aws.rds.DBCluster
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.rds.IntegerOptional AllocatedStorage specifies the allocated storage size in gibibytes (GiB). For Aurora, AllocatedStorage can vary because Aurora DB cluster storage size adjusts as needed.
---@field AvailabilityZones? aws.rds.AvailabilityZones The list of Availability Zones (AZs) where instances in the DB cluster can be created.
---@field BackupRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days for which automatic DB snapshots are retained.
---@field CharacterSetName? aws.rds.String If present, specifies the name of the character set that this cluster is associated with.
---@field DatabaseName? aws.rds.String The name of the initial database that was specified for the DB cluster when it was created, if one was provided. This same name is returned for the life of the DB cluster.
---@field DBClusterIdentifier? aws.rds.String The user-supplied identifier for the DB cluster. This identifier is the unique key that identifies a DB cluster.
---@field DBClusterParameterGroup? aws.rds.String The name of the DB cluster parameter group for the DB cluster.
---@field DBSubnetGroup? aws.rds.String Information about the subnet group associated with the DB cluster, including the name, description, and subnets in the subnet group.
---@field Status? aws.rds.String The current state of this DB cluster.
---@field PercentProgress? aws.rds.String The progress of the operation as a percentage.
---@field EarliestRestorableTime? aws.rds.TStamp The earliest time to which a database can be restored with point-in-time restore.
---@field Endpoint? aws.rds.String The connection endpoint for the primary instance of the DB cluster.
---@field ReaderEndpoint? aws.rds.String The reader endpoint for the DB cluster. The reader endpoint for a DB cluster load-balances connections across the Aurora Replicas that are available in a DB cluster. As clients request new connections to the reader endpoint, Aurora distributes the connection requests among the Aurora Replicas in the DB cluster. This functionality can help balance your read workload across multiple Aurora Replicas ...
---@field CustomEndpoints? aws.rds.StringList The custom endpoints associated with the DB cluster.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the DB cluster has instances in multiple Availability Zones.
---@field Engine? aws.rds.String The database engine used for this DB cluster.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String The version of the database engine.
---@field LatestRestorableTime? aws.rds.TStamp The latest time to which a database can be restored with point-in-time restore.
---@field Port? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The port that the database engine is listening on.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.rds.String The master username for the DB cluster.
---@field DBClusterOptionGroupMemberships? aws.rds.DBClusterOptionGroupMemberships The list of option group memberships for this DB cluster.
---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled, as determined by the BackupRetentionPeriod.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.rds.String The weekly time range during which system maintenance can occur, in Universal Coordinated Time (UTC).
---@field UpgradeRolloutOrder? aws.rds.UpgradeRolloutOrder This data type represents the order in which the clusters are upgraded.
---@field ReplicationSourceIdentifier? aws.rds.String The identifier of the source DB cluster if this DB cluster is a read replica.
---@field ReadReplicaIdentifiers? aws.rds.ReadReplicaIdentifierList Contains one or more identifiers of the read replicas associated with this DB cluster.
---@field StatusInfos? aws.rds.DBClusterStatusInfoList Reserved for future use.
---@field DBClusterMembers? aws.rds.DBClusterMemberList The list of DB instances that make up the DB cluster.
---@field VpcSecurityGroups? aws.rds.VpcSecurityGroupMembershipList The list of VPC security groups that the DB cluster belongs to.
---@field HostedZoneId? aws.rds.String The ID that Amazon Route 53 assigns when you create a hosted zone.
---@field StorageEncrypted? aws.rds.Boolean Specifies whether the DB cluster is encrypted with an Amazon Web Services managed key or a customer managed key.
---@field StorageEncryptionType? aws.rds.StorageEncryptionType The type of encryption used to protect data at rest in the DB cluster. Possible values:
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String If StorageEncrypted is enabled, the Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for the encrypted DB cluster.
