---@field SupportsGlobalDatabases? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether you can use Aurora global databases with a specific DB engine version.
---@field TagList? aws.rds.TagList
---@field SupportsBabelfish? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the engine version supports Babelfish for Aurora PostgreSQL.
---@field SupportsLimitlessDatabase? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the DB engine version supports Aurora Limitless Database.
---@field SupportsCertificateRotationWithoutRestart? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the engine version supports rotating the server certificate without rebooting the DB instance.
---@field SupportedCACertificateIdentifiers? aws.rds.CACertificateIdentifiersList A list of the supported CA certificate identifiers.
---@field SupportsLocalWriteForwarding? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the DB engine version supports forwarding write operations from reader DB instances to the writer DB instance in the DB cluster. By default, write operations aren't allowed on reader DB instances.
---@field SupportsIntegrations? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the DB engine version supports zero-ETL integrations with Amazon Redshift.
---@field ServerlessV2FeaturesSupport? aws.rds.ServerlessV2FeaturesSupport Specifies any Aurora Serverless v2 properties or limits that differ between Aurora engine versions. You can test the values of this attribute when deciding which Aurora version to use in a new or upgraded DB cluster. You can also retrieve the version of an existing DB cluster and check whether that version supports certain Aurora Serverless v2 features before you attempt to use those features.

