---@field Port? aws.rds.Integer The port number that the automated backup used for connections.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.rds.String The Availability Zone that the automated backup was created in. For information on Amazon Web Services Regions and Availability Zones, see Regions and Availability Zones.
---@field VpcId? aws.rds.String The VPC ID associated with the DB instance.
---@field InstanceCreateTime? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the DB instance was created.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.rds.String The master user name of an automated backup.
---@field Engine? aws.rds.String The name of the database engine for this automated backup.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String The version of the database engine for the automated backup.
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String The license model information for the automated backup.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The IOPS (I/O operations per second) value for the automated backup.
---@field StorageThroughput? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The storage throughput for the automated backup.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String The option group the automated backup is associated with. If omitted, the default option group for the engine specified is used.
---@field TdeCredentialArn? aws.rds.String The ARN from the key store with which the automated backup is associated for TDE encryption.
---@field Encrypted? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the automated backup is encrypted.
---@field StorageEncryptionType? aws.rds.StorageEncryptionType The type of encryption used to protect data at rest in the automated backup. Possible values:
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String The storage type associated with the automated backup.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services KMS key ID for an automated backup.
---@field Timezone? aws.rds.String The time zone of the automated backup. In most cases, the Timezone element is empty. Timezone content appears only for Microsoft SQL Server DB instances that were created with a time zone specified.
---@field IAMDatabaseAuthenticationEnabled? aws.rds.Boolean True if mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts is enabled, and otherwise false.
---@field BackupRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The retention period for the automated backups.
---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled, as determined by the BackupRetentionPeriod.
---@field DBInstanceAutomatedBackupsArn? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the replicated automated backups.
---@field DBInstanceAutomatedBackupsReplications? aws.rds.DBInstanceAutomatedBackupsReplicationList The list of replications to different Amazon Web Services Regions associated with the automated backup.
---@field BackupTarget? aws.rds.String The location where automated backups are stored: Dedicated Local Zones, Amazon Web Services Outposts or the Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field MultiTenant? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the automatic backup is for a DB instance in the multi-tenant configuration (TRUE) or the single-tenant configuration (FALSE).
---@field AwsBackupRecoveryPointArn? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the recovery point in Amazon Web Services Backup.
---@field TagList? aws.rds.TagList
---@field DedicatedLogVolume? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV) enabled.
---@field AdditionalStorageVolumes? aws.rds.AdditionalStorageVolumesList The additional storage volumes associated with the automated backup.

