---@field VpcSubnetIds? aws.rds.StringList The EC2 subnet IDs for the DB proxy endpoint.
---@field Endpoint? aws.rds.String The endpoint that you can use to connect to the DB proxy. You include the endpoint value in the connection string for a database client application.
---@field CreatedDate? aws.rds.TStamp The date and time when the DB proxy endpoint was first created.
---@field TargetRole? aws.rds.DBProxyEndpointTargetRole A value that indicates whether the DB proxy endpoint can be used for read/write or read-only operations.
---@field IsDefault? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether this endpoint is the default endpoint for the associated DB proxy. Default DB proxy endpoints always have read/write capability. Other endpoints that you associate with the DB proxy can be either read/write or read-only.
---@field EndpointNetworkType? aws.rds.EndpointNetworkType The network type of the DB proxy endpoint. The network type determines the IP version that the proxy endpoint supports.

