---@field Engine? aws.rds.String Specifies the name of the database engine.
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.rds.Integer Specifies the allocated storage size in gibibytes (GiB).
---@field Status? aws.rds.String Specifies the status of this DB snapshot.
---@field Port? aws.rds.Integer Specifies the port that the database engine was listening on at the time of the snapshot.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.rds.String Specifies the name of the Availability Zone the DB instance was located in at the time of the DB snapshot.
---@field VpcId? aws.rds.String Provides the VPC ID associated with the DB snapshot.
---@field InstanceCreateTime? aws.rds.TStamp Specifies the time in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) when the DB instance, from which the snapshot was taken, was created.
---@field MasterUsername? aws.rds.String Provides the master username for the DB snapshot.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String Specifies the version of the database engine.
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String License model information for the restored DB instance.
---@field SnapshotType? aws.rds.String Provides the type of the DB snapshot.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional Specifies the Provisioned IOPS (I/O operations per second) value of the DB instance at the time of the snapshot.
---@field StorageThroughput? aws.rds.IntegerOptional Specifies the storage throughput for the DB snapshot.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String Provides the option group name for the DB snapshot.
---@field PercentProgress? aws.rds.Integer The percentage of the estimated data that has been transferred.
---@field SourceRegion? aws.rds.String The Amazon Web Services Region that the DB snapshot was created in or copied from.
---@field SourceDBSnapshotIdentifier? aws.rds.String The DB snapshot Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that the DB snapshot was copied from. It only has a value in the case of a cross-account or cross-Region copy.
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String Specifies the storage type associated with DB snapshot.
---@field TdeCredentialArn? aws.rds.String The ARN from the key store with which to associate the instance for TDE encryption.
---@field Encrypted? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the DB snapshot is encrypted.
---@field StorageEncryptionType? aws.rds.StorageEncryptionType The type of encryption used to protect data at rest in the DB snapshot. Possible values:
---@field BackupRetentionPeriod? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The number of days for which automatic DB snapshots are retained.
---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled, as determined by the BackupRetentionPeriod.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.rds.String If Encrypted is true, the Amazon Web Services KMS key identifier for the encrypted DB snapshot.
---@field DBSnapshotArn? aws.rds.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the DB snapshot.
---@field Timezone? aws.rds.String The time zone of the DB snapshot. In most cases, the Timezone element is empty. Timezone content appears only for snapshots taken from Microsoft SQL Server DB instances that were created with a time zone specified.
---@field IAMDatabaseAuthenticationEnabled? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether mapping of Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) accounts to database accounts is enabled.
---@field ProcessorFeatures? aws.rds.ProcessorFeatureList The number of CPU cores and the number of threads per core for the DB instance class of the DB instance when the DB snapshot was created.
---@field DbiResourceId? aws.rds.String The identifier for the source DB instance, which can't be changed and which is unique to an Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field TagList? aws.rds.TagList
---@field SnapshotTarget? aws.rds.String Specifies where manual snapshots are stored: Dedicated Local Zones, Amazon Web Services Outposts or the Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field OriginalSnapshotCreateTime? aws.rds.TStamp Specifies the time of the CreateDBSnapshot operation in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). Doesn't change when the snapshot is copied.
---@field SnapshotDatabaseTime? aws.rds.TStamp The timestamp of the most recent transaction applied to the database that you're backing up. Thus, if you restore a snapshot, SnapshotDatabaseTime is the most recent transaction in the restored DB instance. In contrast, originalSnapshotCreateTime specifies the system time that the snapshot completed.
---@field DBSystemId? aws.rds.String The Oracle system identifier (SID), which is the name of the Oracle database instance that manages your database files. The Oracle SID is also the name of your CDB.
---@field MultiTenant? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Indicates whether the snapshot is of a DB instance using the multi-tenant configuration (TRUE) or the single-tenant configuration (FALSE).
---@field DedicatedLogVolume? aws.rds.Boolean Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV) enabled.
---@field AdditionalStorageVolumes? aws.rds.AdditionalStorageVolumesList The additional storage volumes associated with the DB snapshot. RDS supports additional storage volumes for RDS for Oracle and RDS for SQL Server.
---@field SnapshotAvailabilityZone? aws.rds.String Specifies the name of the Availability Zone where RDS stores the DB snapshot. This value is valid only for snapshots that RDS stores on a Dedicated Local Zone.
---@field FullSnapshotSizeInBytes? aws.rds.LongOptional The full size of the DB snapshot, in bytes.

