---@field PreferredBackupWindow? aws.rds.String The daily time range during which automated backups are created if automated backups are enabled, as determined by the BackupRetentionPeriod parameter. Changing this parameter doesn't result in an outage and the change is asynchronously applied as soon as possible. The default is a 30-minute window selected at random from an 8-hour block of time for each Amazon Web Services Region. For more inform...
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.rds.String The weekly time range during which system maintenance can occur, which might result in an outage. Changing this parameter doesn't result in an outage, except in the following situation, and the change is asynchronously applied as soon as possible. If there are pending actions that cause a reboot, and the maintenance window is changed to include the current time, then changing this parameter causes...
---@field MultiAZ? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether the DB instance is a Multi-AZ deployment. Changing this parameter doesn't result in an outage. The change is applied during the next maintenance window unless the ApplyImmediately parameter is enabled for this request.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.rds.String The version number of the database engine to upgrade to. Changing this parameter results in an outage and the change is applied during the next maintenance window unless the ApplyImmediately parameter is enabled for this request.
---@field AllowMajorVersionUpgrade? aws.rds.Boolean Specifies whether major version upgrades are allowed. Changing this parameter doesn't result in an outage and the change is asynchronously applied as soon as possible.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.rds.BooleanOptional Specifies whether minor version upgrades are applied automatically to the DB instance during the maintenance window. An outage occurs when all the following conditions are met:
---@field LicenseModel? aws.rds.String The license model for the DB instance.
---@field Iops? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The new Provisioned IOPS (I/O operations per second) value for the RDS instance.
---@field StorageThroughput? aws.rds.IntegerOptional The storage throughput value for the DB instance.
---@field OptionGroupName? aws.rds.String The option group to associate the DB instance with.
---@field NewDBInstanceIdentifier? aws.rds.String The new identifier for the DB instance when renaming a DB instance. When you change the DB instance identifier, an instance reboot occurs immediately if you enable ApplyImmediately, or will occur during the next maintenance window if you disable ApplyImmediately. This value is stored as a lowercase string.
---@field StorageType? aws.rds.String The storage type to associate with the DB instance.
